crowded street, sniffed for an instant and then lost again.

122
00:07:56,719 --> 00:08:00,379
'It's coffee,' he murmured, 'real coffee.'

123
00:08:00,379 --> 00:08:05,000
'It's in a Party coffee. There's a whole kilo here,' she said.

124
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:08,120
'How did you manage to get hold of all these things?'

125
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:10,100
'It's all in a Party stuff.

126
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:12,559
There's nothing those swine don't have, nothing.

127
00:08:12,559 --> 00:08:17,120
But of course waiters and servants and people pinch things, and— —look, I got a

128
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:19,459
little packet of tea as well.'

129
00:08:19,459 --> 00:08:24,500
Winston had squatted down beside her. He tore open a corner of the packet.

130
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:27,920
'It's real tea. Not blackberry leaves.'

131
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:30,079
'There's been a lot of tea about lately.

132
00:08:30,079 --> 00:08:33,500
They've captured India, or something,' she said vaguely.

133
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:37,699
'But listen, dear. I want you to turn your back on me for three minutes. Go and sit

134
00:08:37,699 --> 00:08:41,299
on the other side of the bed. Don't go too near the window. And don't turn

135
00:08:41,299 --> 00:08:44,120
around till I tell you.'

136
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:48,620
Winston gazed abstractedly through the muslin curtain. Down in the yard the red

137
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:52,699
armed woman was still marching to and fro between the wash tub and the line.

138
00:08:52,699 --> 00:08:56,779
She took two more pegs out of her mouth and sang with deep feeling:

139
00:08:56,779 --> 00:09:02,840
They say that time heals all things, They say you can always forget; But the smiles

140
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:07,040
and the tears across the ears They twist my art strings yet!

141
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:11,420
She knew the whole dribbling song by heart, it seemed. Her voice floated upward

142
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:16,219
with the sweet summer air, very tuneful, charged with a sort of happy melancholy.

143
00:09:16,219 --> 00:09:19,579
One had the feeling that she would have been perfectly content, if the June

144
00:09:19,579 --> 00:09:23,540
