195
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:33,920
He wondered vaguely whether in the abolished past it had been a normal

196
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:38,840
experience to lie in bed like this, in the cool of a summer evening, a man and a

197
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:42,859
woman with no clothes on, making love when they chose, talking of what they

198
00:12:42,859 --> 00:12:47,238
chose, not feeling any compulsion to get up, simply lying there and listening to

199
00:12:47,238 --> 00:12:52,520
peaceful sounds outside. Surely there could never have been a time when that seemed ordinary?

200
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:58,340
Julia woke up, rubbed her eyes and raised herself on her elbow to look at the oil stove

201
00:12:58,340 --> 00:13:00,620
Half that water's boiled away,' she said.

202
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:04,818
'I'll get up and make some coffee in another moment. We've got an hour. What

203
00:13:04,818 --> 00:13:09,439
